# Repository ownership (issue #129).
#
# Rules governing this file:
#   - Ownership is per-path, most specific match wins. Review by the owning
#     team is REQUIRED on every PR that touches a covered path once branch
#     protection requires code-owner review (see note at the bottom).
#   - The four surfaces below are the places where a wrong merge is expensive:
#     contracts, security and vault code, Provider adapters, and the release
#     workflow. Their owners are separated deliberately so a change cannot land
#     under a vague global owner.
#   - Security-sensitive dependency updates (contracts, adapters, Docker
#     digests, Actions pins) are ALSO excluded from bot merging in
#     .github/dependabot.yml; ownership here is the human-review half of the
#     same guarantee.
#
# Default owner for everything else. Sole maintainer today; expand this line
# before adding contributors so nothing silently lands unowned.
*                                       @monet88

# ---- 1. Contracts (issue #20) ---------------------------------------------
# The stable Public API, its frozen compatibility baselines, the management
# tracer, and the contract tests. A wrong merge here breaks every client.
contracts/                             @monet88
contracts/openapi/                     @monet88

# ---- 2. Security and vault code -------------------------------------------
# Vault, credential handling, tenant isolation, and the authorization
# invariants. A wrong merge here leaks tenants.
apps/gateway/internal/infrastructure/vault/          @monet88
apps/gateway/internal/application/credential.go      @monet88
apps/gateway/internal/application/oauth.go           @monet88
apps/gateway/internal/application/provideraccount*.go @monet88
docs/spec/credential-vault-and-sensitive-data-lifecycle.md     @monet88
docs/spec/provider-account-connection-and-credential-lifecycle.md @monet88
docs/spec/tenant-ownership-authorization-invariants.md         @monet88
docs/spec/tenant-scoped-routing-fallback-affinity-leases.md    @monet88
docs/spec/auth-mode-risk-envelope-and-kill-criteria.md         @monet88
docs/spec/client-api-key-lifecycle-and-admission-controls.md   @monet88

# ---- 3. Provider adapters --------------------------------------------------
# BYOK connectors that hold provider credentials and speak external
# protocols. A wrong merge here is a credential-handling or protocol bug in
# production.
apps/gateway/internal/adapters/        @monet88

# ---- 4. Release workflow (issue #70) ---------------------------------------
# Release, changelog, versioned Docker publishing, GHCR, SBOM, provenance.
# #70 is not merged yet; these patterns are declared now so the release
# workflow cannot land unowned when it does.
/.github/workflows/*release*.yml       @monet88
apps/gateway/Dockerfile                @monet88
apps/gateway/deploy/sandbox/           @monet88

# ---- Meta ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The governance files themselves are owned so a change to ownership or to the
# security policy cannot slip through without review.
/.github/CODEOWNERS                    @monet88
/.github/pull_request_template.md      @monet88
/.github/dependabot.yml                @monet88
/SECURITY.md                           @monet88
/LICENSE                               @monet88
/CONTRIBUTING.md                       @monet88

# NOTE: CODEOWNERS records who must review. GitHub enforces the review once
# branch protection on `main` requires "Require review from Code Owners" and
# "Require status checks to pass before merging". That toggle is a repository
# settings step (issue #129 follow-up), not something a commit can carry.
